          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order identified; event-level conclusion remains unverified\n\nThe relevant manufacturing order is **MO-25-09-1070**, linked to **work order WO-2025-09-004** for the **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine–Dekoven operation.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Work order | **WO-2025-09-004 / MO-25-09-1070** |\n| September cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not determinable from accessible records |\n| Event amount | Not determinable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not determinable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not determinable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot conclude without the event evidence |\n\nThe timestamp is reproduced exactly as recorded; **the source supplies no timezone**.\n\n### Evidence limitation\n\nThe accessible records contain work-order and cost-period data but **no cost-event rows**. The supporting-record service returned **“supporting records not staged,”** and those records are restricted to the records-custodian role. No authorized event summary became available.\n\nTherefore, **I cannot establish whether an event was created after Pending Close**. This is an evidence gap—not a finding that no late event occurred.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B documentation states that newly created transactions falling in the current or a prior period **are not staged or processed after Pending Close until the period is closed or reopened**. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, including those in error. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing.\n\nAccordingly, an ordinary new transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should be held from staging/processing. Its actual recorded status cannot be assessed without its type, creation timestamp, and accounting status.\n\n**Sources:** `work_orders` and `cost_periods` records from `system/oracle_scm_cost_management/state.db`; Oracle policy section “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The evidence-limited report was submitted with state **`needs_evidence`** and saved with provenance at:\n`/cache/work/worker_e99dc37042de/audit-report.json`.",
